# Founder-approved PUBLIC values. This is incomplete and cannot start production.
# This file does not authorize deployment, credentials, DNS changes or purchases.
# Secrets belong in Key Vault references, never in this file or a container image.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://app.warthog.com.au
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=app.warthog.com.au
RESEND_SENDING_DOMAIN=mail.warthog.com.au
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=notifications@mail.warthog.com.au
RESEND_REPLY_TO_ADDRESS=oren@nava-co.com
OPERATOR_EMAIL=oren@nava-co.com
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:oren@nava-co.com
TWILIO_REGION=us1
SMS_MONTHLY_SEGMENT_LIMIT=200
SMS_DAILY_SEGMENT_LIMIT=10

# Resend: Free plan selected. Paid overages/upgrades and tracking must be off.
# These are provider-console settings, not enforced by this environment file.
# Free plan: 100 emails/day and 3,000/month; verified in the provider account.
# Domain verification and live delivery acceptance still await approved public DNS.

# SMS launch countries: AU, US, CA, GB, only after route/registration/STOP tests.
# SMS_COUNTRY_ROUTES_JSON remains unset until actual Messaging Service SIDs exist.
# A$20/month is the SMS budget, not an implemented whole-invoice spending cap.
# Rentals, inbound/replies, carrier charges, tax and redaction must fit the quote.
# No Twilio plan/number purchase until full pricing and entitlement are established.

# Remaining per-recipient/message controls need review alongside provider samples:
# SMS_RECIPIENT_HOURLY_SEGMENT_LIMIT, SMS_RECIPIENT_DAILY_MESSAGE_LIMIT,
# SMS_MAX_SEGMENTS_PER_MESSAGE. Earlier proposals were 4, 3 and 2 respectively.
# Supply all other required settings from docs/production-release.md only after
# the relevant account/credential/market/resource approval. Never add fake secrets
# or a temporary hostname to bypass production readiness.
